# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirects.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# sammiee.dev -> sammyfash.com
#
# The site moved domains in September 2026. This file CANNOT carry that rule on
# Cloudflare Pages: its _redirects only matches paths, never hostnames, so a
# rule written here would be skipped and every old link would quietly keep
# serving the site on the old domain. Two hostnames answering with the same
# pages and no redirect is duplicate content, and it splits whatever ranking
# sammiee.dev has instead of handing it over.
#
# Do it at the edge instead, keeping sammiee.dev registered and pointed at the
# same project:
#
#   Cloudflare  Rules -> Redirect Rules. Match hostname equals sammiee.dev,
#               redirect to concat("https://sammyfash.com", http.request.uri.path),
#               status 301, preserve query string.
#   Netlify     Uncomment the rule below; Netlify does match full URLs here.
#               The trailing ! makes it win over the built page.
#
# 301, not 302: the move is permanent, and only a 301 passes the old domain's
# authority to the new one.
#
# /*  https://sammyfash.com/:splat  301!
#
# Mail is separate from this. Anything still routed at the old domain keeps
# working regardless of what happens to the web traffic.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# /abf-ticketing was live for a few hours on 8 September 2026 as a seventh case
# study before the ticketing work was folded into the festival case as a
# chapter. Without this rule the path falls through to index.html and answers
# 200, which is a soft 404: a crawler that saw the page reads the homepage as
# its new content rather than learning the page moved.
#
# 301 rather than 302, because it is not coming back.
/abf-ticketing   /africa-blockchain-festival   301
/abf-ticketing/  /africa-blockchain-festival   301
